CM_ BO_ 2566554622 "Electrified Accessory Engine Coolant Pump Status
The status of electrified Accessory: Engine Coolant Pump.

See PGN 19456 for the corresponding command message.";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpOperatingStatus "Indicates the operating status of the Engine Coolant Electric Pump system or component.
This parameter is used to inform other devices that this system or component is no longer performing to its operational capacity and that reduced, or no flow, ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpServiceInd "Indicates that service is required for the Engine Coolant Electric Pump system or component.
An active indication may convey a need for component replacement or periodic service. The Engine Coolant Electric Pump Controller Status Reason (SPN 20177) ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpPwr "Calculated electrical power consumed by the Engine Coolant Electric Pump.";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpCtrlTemp "A temperature measured and reported by the device.
It may be used for direct or remote (e.g. by another controller) control of the pump. For example, this may be the temperature of the fluid flowing through the pump, or some other temperature ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpMotorSpd "Motor Speed of the Engine Coolant Electric Pump.";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpCtrlCmdStatus "Indicates the source of the speed command to the Engine Electric Coolant Pump system or component.
00b = Internal Command
01b = External Command
10b = Default Command
11b = Not Available
Note:
00b is communicated when the controller is ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpCtrlStatusReason "Provides the reason code describing the unique failure of the Engine Coolant Electric Pump system or component.
If a detailed reason code is not used by the supporting application, or this reason code is Not Available, the Engine Coolant Electric ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566554622 ElectricPumpEnableStatus "Enable and direction status of the Engine Coolant Electric Pump system or component.

00b = Motor Off
01b = Motor On - Normal, Forward, or Default Direction
10b = Motor On - Reverse Direction
11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2566554366 "Transformer Temperatures
Transformer Temperature Status Message";
CM_ SG_ 2566554366 TwoPhaseWTemp "Indicates the temperature of the Phase W in transformer 2.

Note:  Manufacturer-specific phase nomenclature (e.g. 1,2,3 or a,b,c) may differ.";
CM_ SG_ 2566554366 TwoPhaseVTemp "Indicates the temperature of the Phase V in transformer 2.

