CM_ BO_ 2566569214 "Direct Lamp Control Data 3
This message will be transmitted by the controller that is illuminating the lamps. 

It is not required to be used with PGN 64774.";
CM_ SG_ 2566569214 TransOilPressLowLamp "This parameter provides measured data from the Transmission Oil Pressure Lamp.

00b = Lamp deactivated (Off)
01b = Lamp activated (On)
10b = Error
11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2566569214 TransOilTempHiLamp "This parameter provides measured data from the Transmission Oil Temperature Lamp.

00b = Lamp deactivated (Off)
01b = Lamp activated (On)
10b = Error
11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2566568958 "Direct Lamp Control Command 3
Message that directly controls the driver indicator lamps. See also PGNs 64775 and 64774 for additional lamps and PGN 64188 for the feedback information about these lamps.
Note: Since this message is direct lamp ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568958 TransOilPressLowLamp "Command signal directly controlling the Transmission Oil Pressure Lamp.

00b = Lamp Off
01b = Lamp On
10b = Reserved
11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2566568958 TransOilTempHiLamp "Command signal directly controlling the Transmission Oil Temperature Lamp.

00b = Lamp Off
01b = Lamp On
10b = Reserved
11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2566568702 "EVSE 1 Contactor Status 1
Status of the DC Charging Inlet Contactors, which are used to isolate vehicle's internal DC bus from the EVSE Inlet Connector.
There may be multiple senders of this PG in the system. However, typically each SP will only ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568702 HybDCInletContactor1St "Indicates the state of DC Inlet Contactor 1.

00b = Contactor Open
01b = Contactor Closed
10b = Error- Contactor fault detected
11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2566568702 HybDCChargingBusV "Voltage measured on the HVES side of the DC Charging Inlet Contactors.";
CM_ SG_ 2566568702 HybDCContactorInputV "Voltage measured on the inlet side of the DC Charging Inlet Contactors. 

If provided, this value should be in agreement with SPN 13172 (EVSE Present DC Charging Voltage).";
CM_ BO_ 2566568446 "EVSE 1 Contactor Cmd 1
Command sent to control the DC Charging Inlet Contactors, which are used to isolate vehicle's internal DC bus from the EVSE Inlet Connector.";
CM_ SG_ 2566568446 HybDCInletContactor1Cmd "Contactor command.

00b = Open Contactor
01b = Close Contactor
10b = Reserved
11b = Don't Care / Take no action";
CM_ BO_ 2566568190 "EVSE DC Status 1
This message is sent from the EVCC containing status information receved from the DC EVSE.

If this PG is requested, e.g. using RQST, when no EVSE is connected then specific values or states are provided in each parameter.";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 RespCode "The response code of the EVSE to the last request from the EV.
Typically the values are only significant once current operation progress indicates \"Finished\"
See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.78
0 = OK
1 = OK New Session Established
2 = OK Old ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 ProcessingSt "The progress of the EVSE within its current DC Charging State, as reported by SPN 13171.
For example, if the EVSE is doing a cable check SPN 13171 = 9, Cable check and this SP will indicate 01b, Ongoing. On completion of the cable check this SP ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 IsolStatus "Isolation Status as returned from this instance of EVSE.
The EVSE checks its internal isolation during the Cable Check phase of establishing the DC connection. On completion of the cable check, the value would change from 14 to one of either 0, 1 ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 Status "Status of the DC EVSE as returned from the EVSE
0 = EVSE Not Ready
1 = EVSE Ready
2 = EVSE Shutdown
3 = Utility Interrupt Event
4 = Isolation Monitoring Active
5 = Emergency Shutdown
6 = Malfunction
7 = Reserved
8 = Reserved
9 = Reserved
 ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 PLAchieved "Indicates if the output power from the EVSE has reached the negotiated power limit as determined by the lower of SPN 13161 (EVSE DC Charging Power Maximum) and SPN 13157 (Hybrid DC Charging Power Maximum).
00b = Not limited or no EVSE connected - ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 CurLmtAchieved "Indicates if the output current from the EVSE has reached the negotiated current limit as determined by SPN 13160 (EVSE DC Charging Current Maximum) and SPN 13156 (Hybrid DC Charging Current Maximum).
00b = Not limited or no EVSE connected - see ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 VLmtAchieved "Indicates if the output voltage from the EVSE has reached the negotiated voltage limit as determined by SPN 13159 (EVSE DC Charging Voltage Maximum) and SPN 13155 (Hybrid DC Charging Voltage Maximum).
00b = Not limited or no EVSE connected - see ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 PresentDCChargingCur "High Voltage DC current at the output of the EVSE as measured by the EVSE 

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no current provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.51";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 PresentDCChargingV "High Voltage DC voltage at the output of the EVSE as measured by the EVSE

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no voltage provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.50";
CM_ SG_ 2566568190 ChargingSt "Overall State of the DC charging system
0 = Idle. No EVSE connected
1 = Charging
2 = Standby
3 = Reserved
4 = Power Delivery (Start-up)
5 = Authorizing.  A sub-state of Initializing that could take significant time, therefore the EVCC reports ...";
CM_ BO_ 2566567934 "EV DC Charging Target
This message is sent to the EVCC (and forwarded to the EVSE) and sets the instantaneous limits to be applied during the charge cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 2566567934 TargetChargingCur "Hybrid or Electric vehicle's instantaneous requested DC output current limit.
See also:
SPN 13160 (EVSE DC Charging Current Maximum)
SPN 13164 (EVSE DC Charging Current Minimum)
SPN 13156 (Hybrid DC Charging Current Maximum)
SPN 13169 (DC ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566567934 TargetChargingV "Hybrid or Electric vehicle's instantaneous requested DC output voltage limit.
See also:
SPN 13159 (EVSE DC Charging Voltage Maximum)
SPN 13163 (EVSE DC Charging Voltage Minimum)
SPN 13155 (Hybrid DC Charging Voltage Maximum)
SPN 13170 (DC ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566567934 SequenceCounter "The message counter is used to detect situations where the transmitting ECU malfunction repeats the same frame all the time. The receiver of the information may use the counter parameter to detect this situation. The transmitting device will ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566567934 CRC "The CRC is defined as follows:
• Length: 8 bits
• Polynomial: x^8+x^5+x^3+x^2+x+1
• Initial Value: FFh
• Input Data Reflection: Not reflected
• Result Data Reflection: Not reflected
• XOR value: FFh
SAE makes no claim of the functional safety ...";
CM_ BO_ 2566567678 "EVSE DC Charging Limits 2
This message is sent the from EVCC and reports the minimum charging limits and tolerances of a DC EVSE.";
CM_ SG_ 2566567678 CurRegulationTolerance "Regulated current tolerance of the EVSE.

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no tolerance provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.38";
CM_ SG_ 2566567678 PeakCurRipple "Maximum peak to peak ripple current amplitude on the EVSE output.

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no value provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.48";
CM_ SG_ 2566567678 DCChargingCurMin "Minimum stable DC output current that can be supplied by the EVSE.

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no value provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.45";
CM_ SG_ 2566567678 DCChargingVMin "Minimum stable DC output voltage that can be supplied by the EVSE.

FB00h = Parameter supported, but no value provided by EVSE

See J2847-2 201504 Sect 4.2.46";
CM_ BO_ 2566567422 "EVSE DC Charging Limits 1
