CM_ BO_ 2566605822 "Automated Driving System Status 1
Sent by a controller application which is under control of an automated driving system.";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 VSCtrlOpSt "Used to indicate the operation status of the application responding to the ADS Vehicle Speed Control Command (SPN 15248).
000b = ADS Vehicle Speed Control Command Not Active
001b = Maximum Positive Torque
010b = Normal Mode
011b = Maximum ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 VSCtrlCmdFeedback "This parameter represents the current vehicle speed commanded by the automated driving system (ADS) via ADS Vehicle Speed Control Command (SPN 15248).

Note: 0xFB00 denotes no ADS Vehicle Speed Control is being commanded.";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 SAOfCtrlDeviceForVehSpdCtrlCmd "The receiving application is currently acting upon the ADS Vehicle Speed Control Command (SPN 15248) of the automated driving system (ADS) from this source address.
Note:
254 (FEh) indicates this parameter is supported, but ADS Vehicle Speed ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 VSCtrlCmdReadinessStatus "Used to indicate the recipient's state of readiness for responding to ADS Vehicle Speed Control Command (SPN 15248) of the automated driving system (ADS).

00b = Not Ready
01b = Ready
10b = Error
11b = Not Available";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 TSC1CtrlPurpP7ReadinessStatus "This parameter is used to indicate an application's state of readiness for responding to TSC1 Control Purpose P7 (see SPN 3350) messages.

00b = Not Ready
01b = Ready
10b = Error
11b = Not Available/Not Supported.";
CM_ SG_ 2566605822 SAOfCtrlDeviceForTSC1CtrlPurpP7 "THe source address of the SAE J1939 device that is currently sending a TSC1 message with control purpose P7 that is actively controlling or limiting the power system output.
254 (FEh) indicates this parameter is supported, but no device is ...";
