CM_ BO_ 2566787070 "Language Command
The language message has been defined as a global message to inform all ECUs on the 11783 bus the language that the operator wants to use, the date and time format and the units of measure with which the connected system should ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 DistanceUnitCmd "Command to specify the distance units

00 Metric (km, m, …)
01 Imperial (miles, feet, ..)
10 Reserved
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 AreaUnitCmd "Command to specify the area units

00 Metric (ha or m2)
01 Imperial (acres or feet2)
10 Reserved
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 VolumeUnitCmd "Command to specify the volume units

00 Metric (litre)
01 Imperial (gallon)
10 US (gallon)
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 MassUnitCmd "Command to specify the mass units

00 Metric (tonne, kg, …)
01 Imperial (long tons-UK, pounds, ….)
10 Tons/pounds (short tons-US, pounds, …)
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 DateCmd "Command sent to all ECUs which specifies the displayed order of the date.

0 ddmmyyyy
1 ddyyyymm
2 mmyyyydd
3 mmddyyyy
4 yyyymmdd
5 yyyyddmm
6-255 Reserved";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 DecimalSymbolCmd "Command sent to all ECUs which specifies that a decimal point or Comma should be displayed.

00 Comma is used
01 Point is used
10 Reserved
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 TimeCmd "Command sent to all ECUs which specifies the displayed format of the time

00 24 hour
01 12 hour (am/ pm)
10 Reserved
11 No action";
CM_ SG_ 2566787070 LanguageCodeCmd "Command sent to all ECUs which specifies the operator’s desired language of information.  ISO 11783 shall use the 2-character string country codes in ISO 639.  Typical examples from ISO 639 are: 

Dutch: nl
French: fr
English: en
German: de";
CM_ BO_ 2566786814 "Response for Repetition Rate
This global message is the response of the request of a specific user to change the repetition rate.";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 DataDictionaryRow "This 4 bit parameter indicates the Row that is to be used within the specific Data Dictionary Table identified by the Implement Type. This is the Group (GRUP) in LBS documents.";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 DataDictionaryColumn "This 4 bit parameter indicates the Column that is to be used within the specific Data Dictionary Table identified by the Implement Type. This is the Instance (INST) in LBS documents.";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 ImplementType "This 4 bit parameter indicates which data dictionary page is to be used to locate the identity of the following data.";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 ImplementPos "This 4 bit parameter of this message will indicate which Implement is referenced within a set of identical Implements.  The numbering is to start with 1 at the leftmost, foremost, bottom most implement.  The numbering will then increment from left ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 DataFormat_ErrorCondition "This 2 bit parameter that indicates the format or availability of the data in the following Process Data Parameter.
00 Data format is Long Integer
01 Data format is Floating
10 Data format is unsigned Long Integer
11 Not Available or error
Data ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 ProcessDataType "This 2 bit parameter indicates what the data in the following Process Data Parameters is to be used for. See Table A.2.
00 Data is Set Point
01 Data is Actual values
10 Message is Set Point request
11 Message is Actual value request
Data is Set ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 ProcessDataModifier "This 3 bit parameter that indicates how the data in the following Process Data Parameters is to be used when combined with the Process Data Type parameter. See Table A.2.

NOTE: Process Data Type is included since MOD is a function of PD";
CM_ SG_ 2566786814 RepetitionRateParameter "This parameter defines the repetition rate of the specified PGN.";
