CM_ BO_ 2364558846 "Engine Cylinder 20 Combustion Information
Used to communicate combustion information of Engine Cylinder 20. The PG is transmitted at the end of every combustion in Cylinder 20.";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 MaxPressIncreaseRate "The maximum slope, in degrees of crank angle, of the pressure increase in engine cylinder 20 during the combustion cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 LowFreqKnockLvl "Indicates the level of low frequency knock for engine cylinder 20. This knock occurs at frequencies below the typical knock level reported on SPNs 1371 & 6474.  The level of low frequency knock is reported using a relative scale where 0% is least ...";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 EngCyl20PrssSensorPreliminaryFMI "Used to identify the applicable J1939-73 FMI detected in the engine cylinder 20 pressure sensor.  In the case of multiple failures the most severe is communicated.
A value of 31 is sent to indicate that no failure has been detected or this ...";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 EngCyl20SynchronousKnockLevel "Used to indicate the level of knock for engine cylinder 20. The level of knock is reported using a relative scale where 0% is least level of knock, and increasing levels indicate more knock until 100% indicates the most severe level of knock allowed ...";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 EngCyl20PeakPress "Peak pressure in engine cylinder 20 in combustion cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 2364558846 EngCyl20HeatRelease "The amount of heat produced during combustion in engine cylinder 20.  The negative range is to cover thermodynamic behavior during misfire.";
