CM_ BO_ 2633929470 "Engine Information 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngFuelRackPos "Measured position of the engine fuel rack.  A value of 0% rack represents no fueling and a value of 100% rack represents maximum fueling.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngGasMassFlowRate1 "Gas mass flow rate delivered to an engine through its first fuel control system.  See SPN 3467 for the second fuel control system.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 InstantaneousEstBrakePower "Estimate of the power developed by the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngExhaustGasPress1 "Gage pressure of the exhaust gases as measured at the turbine intake of the turbocharger. This SP to be used for inline engines or exhaust bank 1 of multiple bank engines.  See SPN 5749 for exhaust bank 2 and See SPN 6384 for alternate range and ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngPrefilterOilPress "Gage pressure of the engine oil before the oil reaches the oil filter.   See SPN 7470 for alternate resolution.";
CM_ BO_ 2633937406 "ECU History";
CM_ SG_ 2633937406 TotalECURunTime "Total time accumulated over the life of the ECU, from ignition switch ON to ignition switch OFF.  When the ECU is replaced this value shall be reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937406 TotalECUDistance "Total distance accumulated over the life of the ECU.  When the ECU is replaced this value shall be reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2364541694 "Engine Gas Flow Rate
Flow rates of Air and mixed gasses into the engine cylinders.";
CM_ SG_ 2364541694 TargetFreshAirMassFlow "The intended mass flow rate of fresh air entering the engine air intake, before any EGR mixer, if used.";
CM_ SG_ 2364541694 EngExhstGsRcrcltion2MassFlowRate "Flow rate of gas through the second EGR system. Flow rate of the exhaust gas being recirculated from the 2nd EGR system into combustion air.";
CM_ SG_ 2364541694 EngIntakeAirMassFlowRate "Mass flow rate of fresh air entering the engine air intake, before any EGR mixer, if used.  Flow rate of fresh air conducted to the engine cylinders to support combustion.";
CM_ SG_ 2364541694 EngExhstGsRcrcltion1MassFlowRate "Flow rate of gas through the EGR system. Flow rate of the exhaust gas being recirculated into the combustion air.";
CM_ BO_ 2566810366 "Engine Fuel/Lube Systems";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 FuelPrimingSt "Determination of whether or not the engine fuel system is (or has recently been) sufficiently primed with fuel for starting purposes.
00b = Not sufficiently primed
01b = Sufficiently primed
10b = Unable to determine if sufficiently primed
11b = ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngFuelSupplyPumpIntakePress "Gage pressure of fuel at the fuel supply pump intake.  See Figures SPN16_A & SPN16_B.

See also SPN 1381.";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 FuelPumpPrimerStatus "Parameter used to transmit the actual status of the fuel priming system.  The fuel priming system is a system that purges air in the fuel lines and may assist fuel delivery to a second pump at lower speeds.
00b = Off
01b = On
10b = Error
11b = ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngVentilationStatus "Engine ventilation control states.
000b = Sufficiently vented (all combustible gases have been evacuated from intake and exhaust systems)
001b = Ventilation needed (combustible gases may be present in intake and exhaust systems)
010b = ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngCoolantPreheatedState "Indicates whether the engine coolant is pre-heated sufficiently for starting purposes.
00b = Not sufficiently pre-heated
01b = Sufficiently pre-heated
10b = Unable to determine  engine coolant pre-heated sufficiently
11b = Not available or not ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngOilPreHeatedState "Indicates whether the engine oil pre-heated sufficiently for starting purposes.
00b = Not sufficiently pre-heated
01b = Sufficiently pre-heated
10b = Unable to determine if engine oil is pre-heated sufficiently
11b = Not available or not ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngOilPrimingState "Determination of whether or not the engine is (or has recently been) sufficiently lubricated for starting purposes.
00b = Not sufficiently lubricated
01b = Sufficiently lubricated
10b = Unable to determine if sufficiently lubricated
11b = Not ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngOilPrimingPumpSwitch "Switch input for activating the engine oil priming pump.

00b = Off
01b = On
10b = Error
11b = Not available or not installed";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngOilFilterOutletPress "Oil pressure (gage) measured just downstream of oil filter.Used in conjunction with SPN1208 (pre-filter oil pressure) to determine oil filter health.";
CM_ SG_ 2566810366 EngWasteOilReservoirLevel "Level of crankcase blowby emulsion collected by a container.  Normalized to percent, 0% represents completely empty and 100% represents completely full.";
